cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use terraflux-py in your work, please cite it as below, and cite the papers of the methods you used (see https://sacridini.github.io/terraflux/about/citing/)."
type: software
title: "terraflux-py: Terraflux's Python library for landscape analysis"
abstract: >-
  terraflux-py is the Python library of Terraflux: fast, exact landscape pattern, fragmentation, landscape-metric
  and connectivity analysis (MSPA, landscape metrics, circuit theory, habitat availability indices), conservation
  planning, species distributions and land use change, with the same results as the reference tools, from a single
  raster to maps larger than memory.
authors:
  - family-names: Lacerda
    given-names: Eduardo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3803-5842"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24515396
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24515396
    description: "The concept DOI of terraflux-py on Zenodo: it resolves to the latest version, and each version has its own DOI."
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/sacridini/terraflux-py"
url: "https://sacridini.github.io/terraflux/"
keywords:
  - landscape ecology
  - landscape metrics
  - fragmentation
  - habitat connectivity
  - circuit theory
  - conservation planning
  - species distribution modelling
  - land use and land cover change
  - raster analysis
  - Python
